<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><rss xmlns:a10="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel xml:base="https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/rss/press-releases/"><title>Press releases from Sveriges Riksbank</title><description>Press releases from Sveriges Riksbank as a RSS feed.</description><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 23:30:24 +0200</lastBuildDate><ttl>10</ttl><link>https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/rss/press-releases/</link><item xml:base="https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/esrb-warns-of-vulnerabilities-in-the-financial-system-linked-to-frontier-ai-models/"><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/esrb-warns-of-vulnerabilities-in-the-financial-system-linked-to-frontier-ai-models/</guid><title>ESRB warns of vulnerabilities in the financial system linked to frontier AI models</title><description>The European Systemic Risk Board (ESRB), the EU’s macroprudential oversight authority, is issuing a formal warning regarding vulnerabilities in the financial system linked to frontier AI models. The ESRB's warning calls for relevant authorities to reflect these risks in supervisory and oversight work. </description><pubDate>Tue, 07 Jul 2026 11:30:11 +0200</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-07-07T11:30:11+02:00</a10:updated><link>https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/esrb-warns-of-vulnerabilities-in-the-financial-system-linked-to-frontier-ai-models/</link></item><item xml:base="https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/offline-card-payments--the-options-are-now-expanding/"><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/offline-card-payments--the-options-are-now-expanding/</guid><title>Offline card payments – the options are now expanding</title><description>From today, 1 July 2026, there will be more options for paying by card in-store when buying essential goods. This will strengthen the resilience of the payment system and is based on an agreement between the Riksbank and market participants. </description><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 09:31:02 +0200</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-07-01T09:31:02+02:00</a10:updated><link>https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/offline-card-payments--the-options-are-now-expanding/</link></item><item xml:base="https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/minutes-of-the-monetary-policy-meeting-on-16-june-2026/"><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/minutes-of-the-monetary-policy-meeting-on-16-june-2026/</guid><title>Minutes of the monetary policy meeting on 16 June 2026</title><description>Minutes of the monetary policy meeting on 16 June 2026</description><pubDate>Wed, 24 Jun 2026 09:30:40 +0200</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-06-24T09:30:40+02:00</a10:updated><link>https://www.riksbank.se/en-gb/press-and-published/notices-and-press-releases/press-releases/2026/minutes-of-the-monetary-policy-meeting-on-16-june-2026/</link></item></channel></rss>